    <script type="application/ld+json">
      {"@context":"http://schema.org","@graph":[{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Zivid","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/zividlabs"},"datePublished":"2026-09-10T07:39:35.268Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/zividlabs_vision2026-vision2026-machinevision-activity-7503718804279996416-tzP4","text":"𝐁𝐫𝐢𝐧𝐠𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐦𝐨𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧 𝐭𝐨 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐕𝐈𝐒𝐈𝐎𝐍 𝐭𝐫𝐚𝐝𝐞 𝐬𝐡𝐨𝐰! 👀➡️🦾\n\nWe're heading to #VISION2026 in Stuttgart — and this year we're not just showing you how robots see... but also how they move!\n\n📅 6–8 October\n 📍 Hall 10, Booth 10E53, Messe Stuttgart\n\nAt our booth, you'll get the first live look at 𝒁𝒊𝒗𝒊𝒅 𝑴𝒐𝒕𝒊𝒐𝒏, our new motion planner technology. It plans fast, safe paths straight from the scene your Zivid camera captured — so you can scale robot deployments faster, with less manual programming and shorter integration time.\n\n𝐏𝐞𝐫𝐜𝐞𝐩𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧 𝐰𝐚𝐬 𝐨𝐧𝐥𝐲 𝐡𝐚𝐥𝐟 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐩𝐫𝐨𝐛𝐥𝐞𝐦. 𝐌𝐨𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧 𝐢𝐬 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐧𝐞𝐱𝐭 𝐛𝐚𝐫𝐫𝐢𝐞𝐫 𝐰𝐞'𝐫𝐞 𝐛𝐫𝐞𝐚𝐤𝐢𝐧𝐠. 🚀\n\nYou'll also find our 𝒇𝒖𝒍𝒍 3𝑫 𝒄𝒂𝒎𝒆𝒓𝒂 𝒑𝒐𝒓𝒕𝒇𝒐𝒍𝒊𝒐 running live demos:\n 🔹 Zivid 2+ R-series — surface finishing, assembly, piece picking, and more\n 🔹 Zivid 3 — depalletizing, big bin picking, and other large-volume tasks\n\nDon't forget to bring your own parts if you'd like us to image something specific!\n\n#VISION2026 #MachineVision #3DVision #Robotics #MotionPlanning #IndustrialAutomation VISION - World's leading trade fair for machine vision","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/zividlabs_vision2026-vision2026-machinevision-activity-7503718804279996416-tzP4"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Zivid","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/zividlabs"},"datePublished":"2026-09-09T08:06:28.243Z","headline":"","mainEntityOfPage":"https://kr.linkedin.com/posts/zividlabs_robotguidance-3dvision-machinevision-activity-7503363181621399561-EDF_","text":"Your robot is only as good as the data it sees.🤖\n\nIn this 25-minute webinar, our Field Application Engineer, Yunseo Lee, unpacks the core challenges of industrial robot guidance and how high-performance 3D vision can address them. (English subtitles available.)\n\nYou’ll find answers to questions like:\n\n➡️ Why “just detect the object” isn’t enough for reliable robot guidance\n➡️ The four conditions that challenge 3D vision on the factory floor\n➡️ What real point cloud data looks like in WAAM (wire arc additive manufacturing), sanding, and welding processes\n➡️ Two real-world examples of 3D vision in action\n\nWatch the full webinar here: https://bit.ly/4zZJsgV\n\n#RobotGuidance #3DVision #MachineVision #Robotics #ManufacturingAutomation\n\n-----------------\n\n로봇의 성능은 결국 로봇이 보는 데이터에 달려 있습니다.🤖\n\n이번 25분 웨비나에서는 지비드 코리아의 이윤서 엔지니어가 산업용 로봇 가이던스의 핵심 과제와 이를 고성능 3D 비전으로 해결하는 방법을 소개합니다. (영어 자막 제공)\n\n웨비나에서 다음과 같은 질문에 대한 답을 확인해 보세요.\n\n➡️ 신뢰성 높은 로봇 가이던스를 위해서는 왜 단순히 물체를 검출하는 것만으로 충분하지 않을까요?\n➡️ 실제 공장 환경에서 3D 비전을 어렵게 만드는 네 가지 조건은 무엇일까요?\n➡️ WAAM(와이어 아크 적층 제조), 샌딩, 용접 공정에서 실제 포인트 클라우드 데이터는 어떤 모습일까요?\n➡️ 3D 비전이 실제 산업 현장에서 어떻게 활용되는지 보여주는 두 가지 사례\n\n전체 웨비나는 여기에서 확인하세요: https://bit.ly/4zZJsgV","url":"https://kr.linkedin.com/posts/zividlabs_robotguidance-3dvision-machinevision-activity-7503363181621399561-EDF_"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Zivid","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/zividlabs"},"datePublished":"2026-09-07T08:26:47.740Z","headline":"The sauna and fridge test: Temperature resilience of Zivid 3","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/zividlabs_the-sauna-and-fridge-test-temperature-resilience-activity-7502643521057689600-xZC4","text":"𝐖𝐞 𝐩𝐮𝐭 𝐚 𝐙𝐢𝐯𝐢𝐝 3 𝐜𝐚𝐦𝐞𝐫𝐚 𝐢𝐧 𝐚 75°𝐂 𝐬𝐚𝐮𝐧𝐚. 🔥🔥🔥\n\nLoading docks in winter with the doors wide open, welding cells radiating heat... Temperature swings are everywhere in real production: it can result in 𝐜𝐚𝐥𝐢𝐛𝐫𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧 𝐝𝐫𝐢𝐟𝐭𝐬 and 𝐩𝐨𝐨𝐫 𝐩𝐞𝐫𝐟𝐨𝐫𝐦𝐚𝐧𝐜𝐞 for your 3D camera.\n\nThe datasheet says the optimal temperature range for our Zivid cameras is 0-45°C. Our mad scientist from the Quality and Test team Erik Mørenskog wanted to show you exactly how they perform under extreme temperatures:\n\n ➡️ Capture 1: in a sauna at 75°C (yes, well past our rated 45°C!)\n ➡️ Capture 2: in the walk-in fridge of our canteen at 3°C\n\nWhat did the point clouds look like and how was the calibration under these extreme conditions? Watch the video and find out 👇\n\nLearn more about Zivid 3: https://lnkd.in/dqxwBmZy\n\n#MachineVision #3DVision #Zivid #IndustrialAutomation #Robotics","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/zividlabs_the-sauna-and-fridge-test-temperature-resilience-activity-7502643521057689600-xZC4"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Zivid","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/zividlabs"},"datePublished":"2026-09-02T13:35:52.617Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/zividlabs_machinevision-3dvision-qualitycontrol-activity-7500909364476649472-HFoN","text":"𝐍𝐄𝐖 𝐁𝐋𝐎𝐆 𝐏𝐎𝐒𝐓: 𝐖𝐡𝐚𝐭 𝐢𝐬 3𝐃 𝐃𝐢𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐬𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐥 𝐈𝐧𝐬𝐩𝐞𝐜𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧 (𝐀𝐧𝐝 𝐖𝐡𝐲 𝐈𝐭 𝐌𝐚𝐭𝐭𝐞𝐫𝐬)\n\n🔗 https://lnkd.in/eTWptnTB \n\nA 3d camera that nails inspection in the lab can still make mistakes on the production floor. \n\nOur latest article breaks down what 3D dimensional inspection actually does and what to look for when specifying a camera:\n🔹 Why it comes down to comparing point clouds against CAD to check geometric tolerances\n 🔹 Why trueness matters more than raw resolution (below 0.2 percent, or roughly 0.06mm on a 30cm part)\n 🔹 Where it fits across automotive, aerospace, and foundry work\n 🔹 The cases where 3D inspection is not the right tool\n\n➡️ Read it here: https://lnkd.in/eTWptnTB\n\n#MachineVision #3DVision #QualityControl #Manufacturing #Automation #inspection","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/zividlabs_machinevision-3dvision-qualitycontrol-activity-7500909364476649472-HFoN"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Zivid","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/zividlabs"},"datePublished":"2026-09-01T12:35:38.167Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/zividlabs_can-a-zivid-camera-run-doom-yes-it-can-activity-7500531816492179456-3OcQ","text":"Can a Zivid camera run DOOM? Yes it can!","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/zividlabs_can-a-zivid-camera-run-doom-yes-it-can-activity-7500531816492179456-3OcQ"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"Organization","name":"Zivid","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/zividlabs","address":{"type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Gjerdrumsvei 10A","addressLocality":"Oslo","addressRegion":"Oslo","postalCode":"0484","addressCountry":"NO"},"description":"Zivid is a pure-play provider of structured light-based industrial 3D vision cameras for autonomous industrial robot cells, cobot cells, and other industrial automation systems. The company's primary hardware products are the Zivid 3, Zivid 2+ R-series, Zivid 2+ and Zivid 2 3D color cameras. They are supported by companion software products: the Zivid Software Development Kit (SDK) and the Zivid Studio, a graphical user interface (GUI). ","numberOfEmployees":{"value":101,"@type":"QuantitativeValue"},"logo":{"contentUrl":"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E0BAQFntc0Q6wRRwQ/company-logo_200_200/B4EZ9vdGxZJYAI-/0/1784281328967/zividlabs_logo?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=J8LF5s0XnSno9AXLgsQieA1gN1jjYI0ILAU9GV4LOl4","description":"Zivid","@type":"ImageObject"},"slogan":"Industrial 3D color cameras for pick and place robotics. Random bin picking, piece picking, assembly, machine tending.","sameAs":"https://www.zivid.com"}]}
    </script>
  
  
      
