  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">𝐍𝐄𝐖 𝐁𝐋𝐎𝐆 𝐏𝐎𝐒𝐓: 𝐖𝐡𝐚𝐭 𝐢𝐬 3𝐃 𝐃𝐢𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐬𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐥 𝐈𝐧𝐬𝐩𝐞𝐜𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧 (𝐀𝐧𝐝 𝐖𝐡𝐲 𝐈𝐭 𝐌𝐚𝐭𝐭𝐞𝐫𝐬)

🔗 <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/eTWptnTB?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/eTWptnTB</a> 

A 3d camera that nails inspection in the lab can still make mistakes on the production floor. 

Our latest article breaks down what 3D dimensional inspection actually does and what to look for when specifying a camera:
🔹 Why it comes down to comparing point clouds against CAD to check geometric tolerances
 🔹 Why trueness matters more than raw resolution (below 0.2 percent, or roughly 0.06mm on a 30cm part)
 🔹 Where it fits across automotive, aerospace, and foundry work
 🔹 The cases where 3D inspection is not the right tool

➡️ Read it here: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/eTWptnTB?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/eTWptnTB</a>

