  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="feed-reshare-content__commentary">About a year ago I asked if I could get a <a class="link" href="https://no.linkedin.com/company/zividlabs?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card_reshare-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card_reshare-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Zivid</a> camera to run DOOM on our projector.

I was capable of getting a video of DOOM playing. Extremely low FPS, no actual gameplay…it was definitely due for an update.

Same camera (Zivid 2+ R-Series), roughly the same wall, but this time with much better results! The game is now running on my PC and streaming out through the camera’s projector. Full keyboard control, not just video playback. Average scenes land around 10-15 FPS, with peaks around 35 on simple textures.

This is a personal project, mind you, and definitely not a product recommendation. I imagine there are much more cost-effective ways to play DOOM! 😂  I just like taking our cameras past the jobs we normally ask of them. To experiment and tinker. Frame rate, color palettes, latency, live input. A 30-year-old FPS is a surprisingly honest test. If it gets a few people looking at the automation equipment already on the bench and asking what else they can do with it, even better. A good industry promotes innovation!

I couldn’t in good conscience leave last year’s “can it run DOOM?” thread where it was, and I’m quite happy with the progress!

What should I throw at it next?

<a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fcanitrundoom&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card_reshare-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card_reshare-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#CanItRunDoom</a> <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fzivid&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card_reshare-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card_reshare-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#Zivid</a> <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2F3dvision&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card_reshare-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card_reshare-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#3DVision</a> <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fcamera&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card_reshare-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card_reshare-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#Camera</a> <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fautomation&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card_reshare-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card_reshare-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#Automation</a> <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fnostalgia&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card_reshare-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card_reshare-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#Nostalgia</a> <a class="link" href="